From: ChatGPT <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tcpdump: treat PCAP_CONFIG=no as not found

When cross-compiling under Yocto, AC_PATH_TOOL can leave PCAP_CONFIG set
to the literal string "no".  tcpdump 4.3.0 only checks whether the
variable is non-empty and then attempts to execute it, resulting in:

  ./configure: ...: no: command not found

Normalize the value "no" to an empty string so the existing fallback to
AC_CHECK_LIB(pcap, ...) is used.

---
 aclocal.m4 | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/aclocal.m4
+++ b/aclocal.m4
@@ -1,6 +1,9 @@
 	    # Look for pcap-config.
 	    #
 	    AC_PATH_TOOL(PCAP_CONFIG, pcap-config)
+	    if test "x$PCAP_CONFIG" = "xno"; then
+		PCAP_CONFIG=
+	    fi
 	    if test -n "$PCAP_CONFIG" ; then
 		#
 		# Found - use it to get the include flags for
-- 
